This benchmark operationalizes research and theoretical frameworks from:

  - Buçinca, Z., Malaya, M. B., & Gajos, K. Z. (2021).
    "To Trust or to Think: Cognitive Forcing Functions Can Reduce
    Overreliance on AI in AI-assisted Decision-making."
    Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction.

  - Buçinca, Z. & Gajos, K. Z. (2024).
    "Task-Specific Contrastive Explanations Improve Human Performance
    on AI-Assisted Decision Tasks."

  - Buçinca, Z. et al. (2024).
    "Towards Optimizing Adaptive AI Support: Leveraging Reinforcement
    Learning to Personalize AI Assistance."

  - Buçinca, Z. et al. (2023).
    "AHA!: Facilitating AI Impact Assessment by Generating Examples
    of Harms."

  - Mollick, E. & Mollick, L. (2023).
    Studies on AI productivity effects and workforce skill development.

  - Acemoglu, D. (2024).
    Research on pro-worker AI and complementarity economics.

